 ## Overview
-Niagara Fluids Volume Rendering is a method for rendering volumetric data in Unreal Engine 5 by repurposing the engine's built-in grid-based fluid simulation and rendering pipeline [S1, S2, S3, unofficial]. It ignores the simulation step ("do nothing" simulation) and utilizes only the rendering subsystem to display volume textures [S2, S3, unofficial]. This approach offers native engine integration and flexibility via the material system but is distinguished from its siblings by its reliance on the simulation grid's memory architecture, which imposes severe VRAM constraints and limits effective resolution [S1, S2, unofficial].
